Felipe-

If you go about it the way you describe then you will have to manually insert each of the tikz figures into a tex document, which may or may not be what you want. You wold have to run your code, then have a tex file that was something like:

\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{tikz}

\begin{document}

paragraph...

\includegraphics{example1.pdf}

table...
\end{document}

Alternately, using pgfSweave here is an example Rnw file:


%%%%%%%%%% BEGIN %%%%%%%%%%
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{tikz}
\usepackage{geometry}

\begin{document}

\SweaveOpts{concordance=TRUE}

paragraph...

<<setup,echo=F>>=
library(ggplot2)
@

<<cache=T>>=
d <- ggplot(diamonds, aes(carat, price, fill = ..density..)) +
  xlim(0, 2) + stat_binhex(na.rm = TRUE) + opts(aspect.ratio = 1)
d <- d + facet_wrap(~ color)
@

\begin{figure}[!h]
<<fig=T,external=T, echo=F>>=
print(d)
@
\caption{A figure}
\end{figure}

table...
\end{document}
%%%%%%%%% END %%%%%%%%

This shows off some of the features of pgfSweave. Hope that helps.

-Cameron

